-- access.journey — who may see and do what on repositories, organizations
-- and profiles, walked through the access module's boundaries.
--
-- Fields of entities owned by other modules (accounts/User,
-- repositories/Repository, repositories/RepoUnit, organizations/*) are set in
-- `given` because the grant rules read them; every field a competing grant
-- rule reads is set, so a refusal is a refusal and not an unknown.

-- The common ground: one public user-owned repository, its code unit, its
-- owner, and a stranger.
world {
    cast:
        olga:     accounts/User
        sam:      SignedInUser
        repo:     repositories/Repository
        code:     repositories/RepoUnit
        visitor:  AnonymousVisitor
        internals: ForgeInternals

    given:
        olga.is_admin = false
        olga.is_restricted = false
        olga.visibility = public
        olga.is_active = true
        olga.prohibit_login = false
        sam.is_admin = false
        sam.is_restricted = false
        sam.visibility = public
        repo.owner_user = olga
        repo.owner_org = null
        repo.is_private = false
        repo.is_archived = false
        repo.is_mirror = false
        repo.is_empty = false
        code.repository = repo
        code.kind = code
        code.enabled = true
        code.everyone_access_mode = none
        code.anonymous_access_mode = none
        code.is_external = false
        visitor.channel = web
        internals.name = "repositories"
        -- nobody holds an explicit grant until a journey says so (derived
        -- live, decision 1)
        explicit_unit_mode(olga, repo, code) = none
        explicit_mode(olga, repo) = none
        explicit_unit_mode(sam, repo, code) = none
        explicit_mode(sam, repo) = none
}

journey AnonymousVisitorReadsAPublicRepository {
    goal: Somebody with no account opens a public repository of a public user
          and reads its code; nothing more is asked of them.

    1. the visitor reads the code
        visitor does AnonymousReadsUnit(visitor, code) on AnonymousRepositoryAccess
            creating decision: AccessDecision
        then ReadUnitAnonymously fires
        then decision.basis = anonymous_public

    2. and can see the repository exists
        visitor sees repo.name on AnonymousRepositoryAccess in code

    ends: Public code of a public owner is readable without signing in.
}

journey PrivateRepositoriesDoNotExistForStrangers {
    goal: Olga makes her repository private. An anonymous visitor and Sam, a
          signed-in stranger, both find nothing there; Olga still reads it.

    given:
        repo.is_private = true

    1. the anonymous visitor is refused and is not told the repository exists
        visitor cannot do AnonymousReadsUnit(visitor, code) on AnonymousRepositoryAccess
        visitor cannot see repo.name on AnonymousRepositoryAccess in code

    2. Sam, signed in but with no grant, is refused too
        stipulate explicit_unit_mode(sam, repo, code) = none
        sam cannot do UserReadsUnit(sam, code) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    3. Olga owns it and reads it
        olga does UserReadsUnit(olga, code) on RepositoryUnitAccess
            creating decision: AccessDecision
        then ReadUnitAsRepositoryOwner fires
        then decision.basis = repository_owner

    ends: A private repository is visible to its owner and to nobody without
          a grant; to everyone else it does not exist.
}

journey PrivateProfilesAreSeenOnlyByThoseTheyKnow {
    goal: Pia keeps her profile private. A stranger cannot see it; somebody
          she follows can; an anonymous visitor cannot.

    cast:
        pia: accounts/User

    given:
        pia.is_admin = false
        pia.is_restricted = false
        pia.visibility = private
        follow: accounts/Follow { follower: pia, followee: olga }

    1. Sam, a stranger, is refused
        stipulate shares_organization(pia, sam) = false
        sam cannot do UserViewsProfile(sam, pia) on ProfileAccess
        sam cannot see pia.name on VisibleProfile in pia

    2. the anonymous visitor is refused
        visitor cannot do AnonymousViewsProfile(visitor, pia) on AnonymousProfileAccess

    3. Olga, whom Pia follows, sees her
        olga does UserViewsProfile(olga, pia) on ProfileAccess
            creating decision: AccessDecision
        then ViewPrivateProfileByRelationship fires
        then decision.basis = profile_visible
        olga sees pia.name on VisibleProfile in pia

    4. and everyone always sees themselves
        olga does UserViewsProfile(olga, olga) on ProfileAccess
        then ViewOwnProfileOrAsSiteAdmin fires

    ends: Private means "people I have a relationship with".
}

-- Updated for access decision 1: there is no index to recalculate; the
-- grant counts the moment it exists.
journey ACollaboratorGainsWriteAsSoonAsTheGrantExists {
    goal: Sam can read Olga's public repository but not push to it. Olga adds
          him as a write collaborator; permission is derived from the grant
          itself, so from then on he can write.

    1. before the grant Sam reads but cannot write
        stipulate explicit_unit_mode(sam, repo, code) = none
        stipulate explicit_mode(sam, repo) = none
        sam does UserReadsUnit(sam, code) on RepositoryUnitAccess
        sam cannot do UserWritesUnit(sam, code, true) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    2. the collaboration exists: Sam pushes, with nothing recalculated
        stipulate explicit_unit_mode(sam, repo, code) = write
        stipulate explicit_mode(sam, repo) = write
        sam does UserWritesUnit(sam, code, true) on RepositoryUnitAccess
            creating decision: AccessDecision
        then WriteUnitByExplicitGrant fires
        then decision.basis = explicit_grant

    3. but a write collaborator is not a repository administrator
        sam cannot do UserAdministersRepository(sam, repo) on RepositoryAccessAdministration

    ends: Write comes from an explicit grant, live; administration needs more.
}

-- Updated for access decisions 1 and 7: the removal is seen at once, and
-- the rest of the forge clears what presumed access.
journey RemovingTheLastGrantTakesAccessAway {
    goal: Sam was a write collaborator on Olga's private repository. Olga
          removes him; he loses access at once, and the forge is told so.

    given:
        repo.is_private = true
        collab: repositories/Collaboration { repository: repo, user: sam, access_mode: write }

    1. while the grant stands Sam writes
        stipulate explicit_unit_mode(sam, repo, code) = write
        sam does UserWritesUnit(sam, code, true) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    2. the collaboration is removed and his lost access announced
        stipulate is_repo_admin(olga, repo) = true
        stipulate explicit_unit_mode(sam, repo, code) = none
        stipulate has_any_access(sam, repo) = false
        olga does AdminRemovesCollaborator(olga, repo, collab) on RepositorySettings
        then collab does not exist
        then AnnounceLostAccessOnCollaboratorRemoved fires

    3. and Sam can no longer even read
        sam cannot do UserReadsUnit(sam, code) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    ends: Losing the last grant on a private repository makes it vanish for
          the user, and watches/assignments are cleaned up by their owners.
}

journey GoingPrivateClearsOutsidersWatchesAndSubscriptions {
    goal: Sam watches Olga's public repository, follows one of its issues and
          is assigned to it. Olga makes the repository private; Sam has no
          grant, so he loses read access, and his watch, his issue
          subscription and his assignment are cleared at once (decision 7).

    cast:
        bug: issues/Issue

    given:
        repo.is_fork = false
        repo.fork_of = null
        watch: repositories/Watch { user: sam, repository: repo, source: explicit, watch_issues: true, watch_pull_requests: true, watch_releases: true }
        bug.repository = repo
        bug.assignees = {sam}
        sub: issues/IssueWatch { user: sam, issue: bug, is_watching: true }

    1. Olga makes it private and Sam is told he lost access
        stipulate is_repo_admin(olga, repo) = true
        stipulate repo.owner_is_private = false
        stipulate has_any_access(sam, repo) = false
        stipulate can_be_assigned(sam, repo) = false
        olga does AdminChangesVisibility(olga, repo, true) on RepositorySettings
        then AnnounceLostAccessOnVisibilityChanged fires
        then AnnounceLostAccessAcrossRepository fires
        then UnwatchOnLostAccess fires
        then ClearInvolvementOnLostAccess fires
        then watch.watch_issues = false
        then watch.watch_releases = false
        then sub does not exist
        then bug.assignees = {}

    2. and the repository is gone for him
        stipulate explicit_unit_mode(sam, repo, code) = none
        sam cannot do UserReadsUnit(sam, code) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    ends: Losing read access, for whatever reason, ends what presumed it.
}

journey ArchivedRepositoriesAreReadOnly {
    goal: Olga archives her repository. She can still read it and still
          administer it (she may unarchive), but nobody - not even she - can
          change its content.

    given:
        repo.is_archived = true

    1. reading still works
        olga does UserReadsUnit(olga, code) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    2. pushing does not
        olga cannot do UserWritesUnit(olga, code, true) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    3. Sam cannot open a pull request or comment either
        sam cannot do UserContributesToRepository(sam, code) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    4. administration (e.g. unarchiving) is still allowed
        olga does UserAdministersRepository(olga, repo) on RepositoryAccessAdministration
            creating decision: AccessDecision
        then AdministerRepositoryAsOwner fires

    ends: Archived means read-only for content, not frozen for its owner.
}

journey AMirrorsCodeCannotBePushedButCanBeSynced {
    goal: Olga's repository is a pull mirror. She cannot push to it, but she
          can trigger a sync, which needs write on code without changing it
          by hand.

    given:
        repo.is_mirror = true

    1. a push is refused
        olga cannot do UserWritesUnit(olga, code, true) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    2. "sync now" is a write that does not change git content by hand
        olga does UserWritesUnit(olga, code, false) on RepositoryUnitAccess
            creating decision: AccessDecision
        then WriteUnitAsRepositoryOwner fires

    ends: A mirror's code follows its upstream only.
}

journey RestrictedUsersSeeOnlyWhatTheyAreGiven {
    goal: Rita is a restricted user. A public repository is invisible to her
          until she is given an explicit grant on it.

    cast:
        rita: accounts/User

    given:
        rita.is_admin = false
        rita.is_restricted = true
        rita.is_active = true
        rita.prohibit_login = false

    1. a public repository is still closed to her, and hidden from her
        stipulate explicit_unit_mode(rita, repo, code) = none
        stipulate explicit_mode(rita, repo) = none
        rita cannot do UserReadsUnit(rita, code) on RepositoryUnitAccess
        rita cannot see repo.name on VisibleRepository in repo

    2. she is added as a read collaborator, which counts at once
        stipulate explicit_unit_mode(rita, repo, code) = read
        stipulate explicit_mode(rita, repo) = read
        stipulate has_any_access(rita, repo) = true

    3. and now reads it, through the grant and nothing else
        rita does UserReadsUnit(rita, code) on RepositoryUnitAccess
            creating decision: AccessDecision
        then ReadUnitByExplicitGrant fires
        then ReadUnitByPublicDefault does not fire
        then decision.basis = explicit_grant
        rita sees repo.name on VisibleRepository in repo

    ends: For a restricted user, "public" means nothing; grants mean
          everything.
}

journey PrivateOrganizationsAreVisibleOnlyToMembers {
    goal: A private organization owns a public repository. Sam, who is not a
          member, can see neither the organization nor the repository; Mia,
          a member, can see both.

    cast:
        mia:   SignedInUser
        org:   organizations/Organization
        orepo: repositories/Repository
        ocode: repositories/RepoUnit

    given:
        mia.is_admin = false
        mia.is_restricted = false
        org.visibility = private
        orepo.owner_user = null
        orepo.owner_org = org
        orepo.is_private = false
        orepo.is_archived = false
        ocode.repository = orepo
        ocode.kind = code
        ocode.enabled = true
        ocode.is_external = false
        ocode.everyone_access_mode = none
        ocode.anonymous_access_mode = none
        membership: organizations/OrgMembership { organization: org, user: mia, is_public: false }

    1. Sam cannot see the organization
        sam cannot do UserViewsOrganization(sam, org) on OrganizationAccess
        sam cannot see org.name on VisibleOrganization in org

    2. nor read its public repository
        stipulate explicit_unit_mode(sam, orepo, code) = none
        sam cannot do UserReadsUnit(sam, ocode) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    3. Mia, a member, sees the organization
        mia does UserViewsOrganization(mia, org) on OrganizationAccess
            creating decision: AccessDecision
        then ViewOrganizationAsMember fires
        mia sees org.name on VisibleOrganization in org

    4. and reads its public repository
        stipulate explicit_unit_mode(mia, orepo, code) = none
        mia does UserReadsUnit(mia, ocode) on RepositoryUnitAccess
        then ReadUnitByPublicDefault fires

    ends: Owner visibility gates everything the owner has, even public
          repositories.
}

journey LimitedOrganizationsNeedASignedInViewer {
    goal: A limited organization is visible to any signed-in user but not to
          anonymous visitors.

    cast:
        org: organizations/Organization

    given:
        org.visibility = limited

    1. the anonymous visitor is refused
        visitor cannot do AnonymousViewsOrganization(visitor, org) on AnonymousOrganizationAccess
        visitor cannot see org.name on AnonymousOrganizationAccess in org

    2. Sam, signed in, sees it
        sam does UserViewsOrganization(sam, org) on OrganizationAccess
            creating decision: AccessDecision
        then ViewOrganizationByVisibility fires
        then decision.basis = organization_visible
        sam sees org.name on VisibleOrganization in org

    ends: Limited is "members of this instance only".
}

-- Decision 2: Tom is also a read collaborator; per unit he gets the
-- strongest of that and the unit's team grant - never the team's best grant
-- on every unit.
journey TeamUnitAccessDecidesPerUnit {
    goal: Tom is a read collaborator on a private organization repository and
          in a team that grants write on issues but only read on code. He can
          triage issues and read code, but cannot push.

    cast:
        tom:    SignedInUser
        org:    organizations/Organization
        orepo:  repositories/Repository
        ocode:  repositories/RepoUnit
        tracker: repositories/RepoUnit

    given:
        tom.is_admin = false
        tom.is_restricted = false
        org.visibility = public
        orepo.owner_user = null
        orepo.owner_org = org
        orepo.is_private = true
        orepo.is_archived = false
        orepo.is_mirror = false
        orepo.is_empty = false
        ocode.repository = orepo
        ocode.kind = code
        ocode.enabled = true
        ocode.is_external = false
        ocode.everyone_access_mode = none
        ocode.anonymous_access_mode = none
        tracker.repository = orepo
        tracker.kind = issues
        tracker.enabled = true
        tracker.is_external = false
        tracker.everyone_access_mode = none
        tracker.anonymous_access_mode = none
        collab: repositories/Collaboration { repository: orepo, user: tom, access_mode: read }

    1. per unit, the strongest of his read collaboration and the team's unit grant
        stipulate explicit_unit_mode(tom, orepo, issues) = write
        stipulate explicit_unit_mode(tom, orepo, code) = read

    2. Tom triages issues
        tom does UserWritesUnit(tom, tracker, false) on RepositoryUnitAccess
            creating decision: AccessDecision
        then WriteUnitByExplicitGrant fires

    3. reads code
        tom does UserReadsUnit(tom, ocode) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    4. but cannot push
        tom cannot do UserWritesUnit(tom, ocode, true) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    ends: On organization repositories a team's unit access, not its overall
          mode, decides each unit.
}

journey AdminTeamsAdministerButOnlyOwnersDelete {
    goal: Ada is in an admin team, Otto in the owner team of the organization
          owning a repository. Both administer it; only Otto may delete or
          transfer it.

    cast:
        ada:   SignedInUser
        otto:  SignedInUser
        org:   organizations/Organization
        orepo: repositories/Repository

    given:
        ada.is_admin = false
        otto.is_admin = false
        orepo.owner_user = null
        orepo.owner_org = org

    1. Ada administers the repository
        stipulate explicit_mode(ada, orepo) = admin
        stipulate explicit_mode(otto, orepo) = owner
        ada does UserAdministersRepository(ada, orepo) on RepositoryAccessAdministration
        then AdministerRepositoryByExplicitGrant fires

    2. but cannot delete it
        ada cannot do UserPerformsOwnerAction(ada, orepo) on RepositoryAccessAdministration

    3. Otto, in the owner team, can
        otto does UserPerformsOwnerAction(otto, orepo) on RepositoryAccessAdministration
            creating decision: AccessDecision
        then OwnRepositoryAsOwnerTeamMember fires

    ends: Admin is everything but the irreversible ownership actions.
}

journey AFineGrainedTokenNarrowsEvenAnAdministrator {
    goal: Ash is a site administrator using a token restricted to public
          repositories. Through it he can read public code but cannot touch a
          private repository nor use administrator powers.

    cast:
        ash:   accounts/User
        token: CredentialRestriction
        prepo: repositories/Repository
        pcode: repositories/RepoUnit

    given:
        ash.is_admin = true
        ash.is_restricted = false
        ash.is_active = true
        ash.prohibit_login = false
        token.reach = public_only
        token.has_admin_scope = false
        prepo.owner_user = olga
        prepo.owner_org = null
        prepo.is_private = true
        prepo.is_archived = false
        prepo.is_mirror = false
        pcode.repository = prepo
        pcode.kind = code
        pcode.enabled = true
        pcode.is_external = false
        pcode.everyone_access_mode = none
        pcode.anonymous_access_mode = none

    1. he reads public code through the token, as any user would
        stipulate explicit_unit_mode(ash, repo, code) = none
        ash does UserReadsUnit(ash, code, token) on RepositoryUnitAccess
        then ReadUnitByPublicDefault fires
        then ReadUnitAsSiteAdmin does not fire

    2. a private repository is out of the token's reach
        ash cannot do UserWritesUnit(ash, pcode, true, token) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    3. and the token confers no administrator override
        ash cannot do UserActsAsSiteAdmin(ash, token) on SiteAdministration

    4. without the token he is an administrator again
        ash does UserActsAsSiteAdmin(ash) on SiteAdministration
            creating decision: AccessDecision
        then ActAsSiteAdmin fires

    ends: A credential restriction only ever narrows.
}

journey BlockedUsersCannotContribute {
    goal: Olga has blocked Sam. He can still read her public repository, but
          cannot open issues, comment or react there.

    given:
        block: accounts/UserBlock { blocker: olga, blocked: sam }

    1. Olga's block is in place
        then block exists

    2. Sam still reads
        sam does UserReadsUnit(sam, code) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    3. but cannot contribute
        sam cannot do UserContributesToRepository(sam, code) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    ends: Blocking stops participation, not reading public content.
}

journey AForkPullRequestRunIsReadOnly {
    goal: A workflow run triggered by a pull request from a fork reads the
          repository it runs in but cannot write to it; a normal run can.

    cast:
        forkrun:   RunningTask
        normalrun: RunningTask
        run:       actions/WorkflowRun
        job:       actions/Job

    given:
        run.repository = repo
        job.run = run
        forkrun.job = job
        forkrun.status = running
        forkrun.is_fork_pull_request = true
        normalrun.job = job
        normalrun.status = running
        normalrun.is_fork_pull_request = false

    1. the fork run reads
        forkrun does ActionsTaskAccessesRepository(forkrun, code, read) on ActionsTaskAccess

    2. but cannot write
        forkrun cannot do ActionsTaskAccessesRepository(forkrun, code, write) on ActionsTaskAccess

    3. the normal run writes
        normalrun does ActionsTaskAccessesRepository(normalrun, code, write) on ActionsTaskAccess
            creating decision: AccessDecision
        then TaskAccessesOwnRepository fires
        then decision.basis = own_task

    ends: Untrusted code from forks never gets write.
}

journey ASiteAdminsTokenNeedsTheAdminScope {
    goal: Ash, a site administrator, holds two tokens reaching every
          repository; only one carries the admin scope. Through the other he
          is an ordinary user: Olga's private repository is closed to him and
          the admin endpoints refuse him (decision 5).

    cast:
        ash:     accounts/User
        plain:   CredentialRestriction
        admintok: CredentialRestriction

    given:
        ash.is_admin = true
        ash.is_restricted = false
        ash.is_active = true
        ash.prohibit_login = false
        plain.reach = all_repositories
        plain.has_admin_scope = false
        admintok.reach = all_repositories
        admintok.has_admin_scope = true
        repo.is_private = true

    1. without the admin scope he cannot read the private repository
        stipulate explicit_unit_mode(ash, repo, code) = none
        ash cannot do UserReadsUnit(ash, code, plain) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    2. nor administer it, nor the instance
        stipulate explicit_mode(ash, repo) = none
        ash cannot do UserAdministersRepository(ash, repo, plain) on RepositoryAccessAdministration
        ash cannot do UserActsAsSiteAdmin(ash, plain) on SiteAdministration

    3. with the admin scope he reads it as a site administrator
        ash does UserReadsUnit(ash, code, admintok) on RepositoryUnitAccess
            creating decision: AccessDecision
        then ReadUnitAsSiteAdmin fires
        then decision.basis = site_admin

    4. and uses the admin endpoints
        ash does UserActsAsSiteAdmin(ash, admintok) on SiteAdministration
        then ActAsSiteAdmin fires

    ends: The token limits everything; admin powers need the admin scope.
}

journey ATaskTokenStaysInItsRepository {
    goal: A normal workflow run reads and writes the repository it runs in,
          but its token cannot even read another public repository
          (decision 6).

    cast:
        task:   RunningTask
        run:    actions/WorkflowRun
        job:    actions/Job
        other:  repositories/Repository
        ocode:  repositories/RepoUnit

    given:
        run.repository = repo
        job.run = run
        task.job = job
        task.status = running
        task.is_fork_pull_request = false
        other.owner_user = olga
        other.owner_org = null
        other.is_private = false
        other.is_archived = false
        ocode.repository = other
        ocode.kind = code
        ocode.enabled = true
        ocode.is_external = false

    1. the task reads its own repository
        task does ActionsTaskAccessesRepository(task, code, read) on ActionsTaskAccess
        then TaskAccessesOwnRepository fires

    2. but not another one, public as it is
        task cannot do ActionsTaskAccessesRepository(task, ocode, read) on ActionsTaskAccess

    ends: A job token is repository-scoped.
}

journey APrivateRepositoryWithAPublicIssueTracker {
    goal: Olga keeps her repository private but opens its issue tracker to
          everyone. Visitors read the issues - only the issues - and nobody
          without a grant may write there (decisions 3 and 4).

    cast:
        tracker: repositories/RepoUnit

    given:
        repo.is_private = true
        tracker.repository = repo
        tracker.kind = issues
        tracker.enabled = true
        tracker.is_external = false
        tracker.everyone_access_mode = none
        tracker.anonymous_access_mode = none

    1. an anonymous default of write is refused
        stipulate is_repo_admin(olga, repo) = true
        olga cannot do AdminSetsUnitDefaultAccess(olga, repo, tracker, write, write) on RepositorySettings

    2. Olga makes the tracker public: read for visitors, write for signed-in users
        stipulate has_any_access(olga, repo) = true
        olga does AdminSetsUnitDefaultAccess(olga, repo, tracker, write, read) on RepositorySettings
        then tracker.anonymous_access_mode = read
        then tracker.everyone_access_mode = write

    3. an anonymous visitor reads the issues but not the code
        visitor does AnonymousReadsUnit(visitor, tracker) on AnonymousRepositoryAccess
            creating decision: AccessDecision
        then ReadUnitAnonymously fires
        visitor cannot do AnonymousReadsUnit(visitor, code) on AnonymousRepositoryAccess

    4. Sam, signed in, reads the issues and sees the repository
        stipulate explicit_unit_mode(sam, repo, issues) = none
        stipulate explicit_unit_mode(sam, repo, code) = none
        stipulate explicit_mode(sam, repo) = none
        sam does UserReadsUnit(sam, tracker) on RepositoryUnitAccess
        then ReadUnitByPublicDefault fires
        sam sees repo.name on VisibleRepository in repo

    5. but not the code, and he cannot triage: a private repository's public unit is read-only
        sam cannot do UserReadsUnit(sam, code) on RepositoryUnitAccess
        sam cannot do UserWritesUnit(sam, tracker, false) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    ends: Units, not only repositories, can be public.
}

journey AUnitDefaultLetsEveryoneWrite {
    goal: On Olga's public repository the projects board lets every signed-in
          user write; Sam edits it, but a restricted user may not (decision 4).

    cast:
        board: repositories/RepoUnit
        rita:  accounts/User

    given:
        board.repository = repo
        board.kind = projects
        board.enabled = true
        board.is_external = false
        board.everyone_access_mode = write
        board.anonymous_access_mode = none
        rita.is_admin = false
        rita.is_restricted = true
        rita.is_active = true
        rita.prohibit_login = false

    1. Sam, with no grant, writes on the board
        stipulate explicit_unit_mode(sam, repo, projects) = none
        sam does UserWritesUnit(sam, board, false) on RepositoryUnitAccess
            creating decision: AccessDecision
        then WriteUnitByEveryoneWritable fires
        then decision.basis = everyone_writable

    2. but not on the code, which keeps the default
        stipulate explicit_unit_mode(sam, repo, code) = none
        sam cannot do UserWritesUnit(sam, code, false) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    3. and a restricted user gets nothing from the default
        stipulate explicit_unit_mode(rita, repo, projects) = none
        rita cannot do UserWritesUnit(rita, board, false) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    ends: "Everyone may write" is a per-unit setting, no longer the wiki's alone.
}

-- decided: administration 3 — while the instance is read-only every write is
-- refused, the owner's and a site admin's included; reads keep working.
journey ReadOnlyModeRefusesEveryWrite {
    goal: The site administrator has put the instance into read-only mode for
          a backup. Olga can still read her repository, but she cannot push,
          and Sam cannot comment or open a pull request.

    cast:
        gate: InstanceWriteGate

    given:
        gate.read_only = true
        gate.message = "Backup in progress"

    1. reading still works
        olga does UserReadsUnit(olga, code) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    2. the owner's push is refused
        olga cannot do UserWritesUnit(olga, code, true) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    3. nor can Sam contribute
        sam cannot do UserContributesToRepository(sam, code) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    ends: Nothing changes while the instance is read-only.
}

-- decided: follow-up 1 (site admins keep implicit read, but a read of a
-- private repository they hold no role in is audited)
journey ASiteAdminReadsAPrivateRepositoryAndIsRecorded {
    goal: Ash, a site administrator with no role in Olga's private
          repository, opens its code. He may read it, and the read is
          recorded for audit. Reading a private repository he collaborates
          on leaves no audit record.

    cast:
        ash:   accounts/User
        crepo: repositories/Repository
        ccode: repositories/RepoUnit

    given:
        ash.is_admin = true
        ash.is_restricted = false
        ash.is_active = true
        ash.prohibit_login = false
        repo.is_private = true
        explicit_unit_mode(ash, repo, code) = none
        explicit_mode(ash, repo) = none
        crepo.owner_user = olga
        crepo.owner_org = null
        crepo.is_private = true
        crepo.is_archived = false
        crepo.is_mirror = false
        ccode.repository = crepo
        ccode.kind = code
        ccode.enabled = true
        ccode.is_external = false
        ccode.everyone_access_mode = none
        ccode.anonymous_access_mode = none
        explicit_unit_mode(ash, crepo, code) = read
        explicit_mode(ash, crepo) = read

    1. a stranger still cannot read the private repository
        sam cannot do UserReadsUnit(sam, code) on RepositoryUnitAccess

    2. Ash reads it on the strength of being an administrator, and it is logged
        ash does UserReadsUnit(ash, code) on RepositoryUnitAccess
            creating record: AdminAccessRecord
        then ReadUnitAsSiteAdmin fires
        then RecordSiteAdminReadWithoutRole fires
        then record.admin = ash
        then record.repository = repo
        then record.unit_kind = code

    3. where he collaborates, his read needs no audit
        ash does UserReadsUnit(ash, ccode) on RepositoryUnitAccess
        then ReadUnitByExplicitGrant fires
        then ReadUnitAsSiteAdmin fires
        then RecordSiteAdminReadWithoutRole does not fire

    ends: Administrators can open any repository; every role-less read of a
          private one leaves an audit record.
}
